name issue_356_capacity_drop_xr_rtt
describe capacity_drop with quality scaling on, seed 1: the receiver measures its RTT over XR RRTR/DLRR as libwebrtc's does, so its NACK retries and the repair after the drop match (#356)
duration 40s
quality_scaling on
seed 1
at 0s  capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=400ms
at 10s capacity=500kbps
at 25s capacity=2500kbps
# Seed 1 is one of #356's yardstick seeds (#358). Before the drop the receiver's RTT comes from the DLRR echoes,
# which see a short forward queue, so it retries NACKs every 80 ms as libwebrtc's does (ours was 100 ms with the
# sender's RR samples). The repair after the drop then ends past libwebrtc's 3 s kMaxWaitForFrame and the
# receiver asks for a keyframe, as libwebrtc's does on this seed.
# libwebrtc seed 1 (parity-data @ 308b957): keyframe_requests 1, longest freeze 3031 ms.
# main @ 4a21d1b (#366): 0, 1700 ms. With the port: 1, 3095 ms.
# This scenario used seed 2 until #366 merged; with #366 seed 2 no longer reaches the timeout (0, 1624 ms;
# libwebrtc 1, 3103 ms). On seeds 1-10 the port still moves both cells toward libwebrtc (see #361).
# PR #381 (#365): `video.keyframe_requests >= 1` deleted (Owner, 2026-10-25 9:32 AM PT). Whether the repair after the
# drop reaches the receiver's 3 s kMaxWaitForFrame is a single-seed yes/no: libwebrtc misses it on 5 of seeds 1-10
# (keyframe_requests 1,1,0,0,1,0,0,1,1,0), so no bound under the tight rule checks anything (its floor is >= 0).
# longest_freeze_ms below stays the scenario's lock.
# PR #381 (#365, 1 ms feedback receive times and nearest-tick transport-cc deltas, as libwebrtc; program.md 0.2, Owner sign-off
# 2026-10-25 8:49 AM PT, tight rule; not a gap on the means): was > 2500. Ours 2306 on seed 1 (mean 2398);
# libwebrtc seed 1 3031, worst of seeds 1-10 1253 (mean 2688; fails > 2500 on 3 of 10). About 12 % below ours, above libwebrtc's worst.
# #655 (the frame dropper and the bitrate adjuster get the size sent after the keyframe SPS VUI rewrite, +5 B, as
# libwebrtc's VideoStreamEncoder::RunPostEncode; program.md 0.2 guard rail, tight rule): was > 2030. Ours on seeds
# 1-10 (main 5a50470 -> this change): 2411 1752 1801 2712 3168 3161 3044 3100 3206 2762 (mean 2692) ->
# 1962 1752 1801 2712 3167 3131 3044 3100 1827 2762 (mean 2526). libwebrtc (parity-data, M157): 1899 3177 2502 3044
# 1805 3116 1688 3128 1623 2785 (mean 2477, worst 1623). 13 % below ours on seed 1, above libwebrtc's worst.
expect video.longest_freeze_ms > 1700
